|rarity = RR
|name1 = Awa-Odori Cat
|name2 = So-Ran Cat
|name3 = Gorgeous Groovin' Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''So-Ran Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gorgeous Groovin' Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, it can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of cats able to perform this role without relevant differences. Awa-Odori Cat, however, can be used in {{4c}} or specific [[Wrath of D-Cyclone (Insane)|restriction stages,]] where there is considerably less competition. Awa-Odori Cat can also be used on certain stages where you would need a lot of cheap meatshields such as [[Drunken Backrub]].

Awa-Odori Cat can be used as a slightly faster [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]] in {{4c}} stages but might be overshadowed by [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]], [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]], or [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]].

If one is to own [[Trickster Himeyuri (Uber Rare Cat)|Trickster Himeyuri]] and [[Vengeful Cat (Rare Cat)|Vengeful Cat]], Awa-Odori Cat can be used along with them to activate the [[Kimono Champs (Combo)|Kimono Champs]] combo, which is a very slot efficient Research (L) combo, and you can use Awa-Odori Cat as an extra meatshield.

==='''True Form'''===
Gorgeous Groovin' Cat gains a little health & damage, along with the Behemoth Slayer ability, with a slightly higher [[Dodge Attack|Dodge]] chance than usual. This stat increase can be completely ignored, however, as it does nothing for this unit. Against Behemoths, it can help as an extra meatshield with a chance to dodge, but the chance is too low to be relied upon for the high evolution cost. For this reason, it's better to save Behemoth Stones for other, more powerful units.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield & Combo Slave}}

